    <section class="py-16 md:py-20 bg-white">
      <div class="container mx-auto px-4">
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto">
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-6 text-slate-900">ISO 17025 accreditation in a works container: checklist for DAkkS assessment</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">ISO/IEC 17025:2017 puts technical competence and reproducible environmental conditions at the centre, not construction method. DAkkS assessors typically check in works containers: climate-controlled measuring rooms with documented temperature ±0.5 K and humidity 40–60 % rH ±5 % (VDI/VDE 2627 class 3), vibration spectrum at the measuring position (VC-D or VC-E for microbalances), EMC field strength ≤3 V/m for sensitive instruments, traceability of all measuring equipment to national standards via accredited DKD calibration, method validation to ISO 17025 clause 7.2, impartiality evidence.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Frequent defects at first assessment: missing 24/7 climate recording, no vibration measurement before instrument installation, EMC shielding without a field-strength record, LIMS without an audit trail. Planexus supplies a DAkkS-ready pack: environmental qualification protocol, Pt100 loggers with DKD calibration, vibration measurement protocol with VC curve, EMC pre-test to EN 55011, sample method validation for tensile testing to DIN EN ISO 6892 and hardness testing to DIN EN ISO 6507.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-8">Re-accreditation every 5 years, surveillance assessment annually. Container hire agreements of 36–60 months with annual re-qualification of environmental conditions in the hire contract keep the audit trail unbroken – re-qualification cost: €2,500–4,500 per year.</p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-heading font-bold mb-6 text-slate-900">Vibration isolation for microbalances in a container: limit values to VC curves</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Microbalances (resolution 0.01–0.1 mg) respond to floor vibration from 0.1 µm/s. VC curves (Vibration Criteria) define limit values: VC-D for microbalances ≤3 µm/s (1/3-octave band 8–80 Hz), VC-E for SEM ≤1.5 µm/s. Works-hall floors without isolation: typically 20–100 µm/s – unsuitable. Container solution: spring foundation with natural frequency &lt;2 Hz, optional pneumatic isolation, 200 mm granite plate on rubber-metal mounts, separate foundation slab decoupled from the container frame.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Measurement before commissioning: vibration spectrum at four corners of the granite plate, comparison with the VC target curve, documentation for the DAkkS audit. Vibration-isolation cost: €15,000–45,000 depending on the mass of a universal testing machine (250 kN) or microbalance. EMC shielding (mu-metal wall, ≤3 V/m) is added for SEM and NMR spectrometers on a project basis at €20,000–60,000. For steelworks with blast-furnace vibration we plan additional decoupling of the container foundation from the hall floor. We repeat the measurement after each DAkkS surveillance assessment.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">Series testing on the production line: QC containers with MES/ERP connection via OPC UA to common systems. Test results are stored by batch; limit exceedances trigger a batch hold. Payback versus an external testing laboratory is typically 18–24 months at ≥200 samples/day and three-shift operation.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4">A maintenance contract with annual DAkkS re-qualification of environmental conditions is available as an option. For automotive suppliers under IATF 16949 we supply PPAP documentation and measuring-equipment lists as an annex to the container handover protocol. Works QC containers can be linked to existing test plans to DIN EN ISO 6892, ISO 6507 and ISO 6508. Typical lead time from the Albstadt factory: 10–14 weeks including DAkkS-ready qualification, factory acceptance FAT and SAT on site available as an option.</p>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-8">Fuel quality, refinery turnaround, H₂S and tank-farm environmental analytics sit on the <a href="/en/industries/oil-gas" class="text-primary font-medium hover:underline">oil, gas &amp; refining</a> page – not in materials QC.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

